    "part": "PART XIV — SERVICES UNDER THE UNION AND THE STATES",
    "title": "Article 311: Dismissal, Removal, or Reduction in Rank",
    "definition": "(1) No civil servant shall be dismissed or removed by an authority subordinate to their appointing authority. (2) No such person shall be dismissed, removed, or reduced in rank except after an inquiry in which they have been informed of the charges and given a reasonable opportunity of being heard. (3) Exceptions: (a) where the person is dismissed on conviction for a criminal offence; (b) where the authority is satisfied that an inquiry is not reasonably practicable; (c) where the President/Governor is satisfied that retention is prejudicial to national security.",
